<article class="env-lemma" id="0AHV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AHV">Lemma <span data-tag="0AHV">80.5.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $F : (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}^{opp} \to \textit{Sets}$ be a functor. Let $X$ be a scheme and let $X \to F$ be representable by algebraic spaces and locally quasi-finite. Then $X \to F$ is representable (by schemes). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $T$ be a scheme and let $T \to F$ be a morphism. We have to show that the algebraic space $X \times _ F T$ is representable by a scheme. Consider the morphism 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X \times _ F T \longrightarrow X \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{Z})} T  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since $X \times _ F T \to T$ is locally quasi-finite, so is the displayed arrow (Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03XN" data-tag="03XN">67.27.8</a>). On the other hand, the displayed arrow is a monomorphism and hence separated (Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/042N" data-tag="042N">67.10.3</a>). Thus $X \times _ F T$ is a scheme by Morphisms of Spaces, Proposition <a href="/tag/03XX" data-tag="03XX">67.50.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>